            <ArticleTitle>Pain management of chronic nonmalignant neuropathic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>387-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic nonmalignant neuropathic pain is difficult to manage. A challenging case dealing with chronic neuropathic pain subsequent to thoracotomy syndrome and reflex sympathetic dystrophy syndrome is presented. Strategies and approaches to aggressively manage this type of pain are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
